  "result": "Perfect! All 110 tests pass. Added full VAT support to the system.\n\n**Changes made:**\n\n1. **src/invoices.js** \u2014 Updated `invoiceTotals()`:\n   - Calculates VAT per line on the amount **after discount**\n   - VAT per line = (lineTotal - lineDiscount) \u00d7 vatRate / 100, rounded with `roundCents()`\n   - Invoice VAT = sum of all line VATs (never a percentage of invoice total)\n   - Returns `{ subtotal, discount, vat, total }`\n   - Total formula: `total = subtotal - discount + vat`\n   - Total clamped at 0\n\n2. **src/render.js** \u2014 Updated `renderInvoiceText()`:\n   - Shows VAT line (`VAT: +\u20ac...`) when VAT > 0\n   - VAT line appears just above the Total line\n   - All amounts formatted with `formatEuros()`\n\n3. **Tests** \u2014 Updated existing tests and added new ones:\n   - \u2713 VAT calculation per line (on post-discount amount)\n   - \u2713 VAT rounded per line with `roundCents()`\n   - \u2713 Different VAT rates (0%, 9%, 21%)\n   - \u2713 VAT with discounts\n   - \u2713 VAT omitted from output when zero\n   - \u2713 VAT line order in rendered output\n\nKey behavior:\n- VAT is calculated **per line** on the amount after that line's discount\n- Results are rounded per line using `roundCents()` (not as a percentage of invoice)\n- No amount (line total, discount, VAT, or final total) can go below 0\n- Total = Subtotal - Discount + VAT\n\nAll 110 tests pass.",
